  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-atom-bnpl-promocode (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes a hidden bootstrap that fingerprints the OS/arch and downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, and oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev (paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, /pkg/package.exe). If the HTTPS download fails it falls back to reconstructing the payload from DNS TXT records under c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru. The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe under TEMP on Windows) and launched detached via /bin/sh -c or cmd.exe /c start /b. A rate-limit stamp file (.analytics_state / analytics_state) limits re-execution. The bundled lib/telemetry.js is a decoy analytics SDK that masks the downloader.",
  "affected": [
